    76	## 1. Profile identity
    77	
    78	- **Profile id:** `tessera-v1-strict`. It appears in the signed bytes as `common.profile` and in the DNS and git
    79	  record as `profile=`. [ENC §3.2:264; ENC §7:569; A9:142]
    80	- **Spec binding:** `common.spec.id` is `tessera-v1-strict/verification-spec/1` and `common.spec.sha256` is the hash
    81	  of the specification bytes. [ENC §3.2:265-266]
    82	  - `common.spec.id` other than that value gives `INVALID / SPEC_ID`. The verifier compiles in a **frozen spec
    83	    catalog**; a `common.spec.sha256` not in it gives `UNVERIFIABLE / SPEC_UNKNOWN`. The signed `vectors_sha256` and
    84	    `preamble_sha256` must equal the catalog entry (`INVALID / SPEC_OBJECT_MISMATCH`), and the bundled `spec`,
    85	    `vectors`, `preamble` and `dependency_manifest` bytes must hash to their signed or catalog values
    86	    (`INVALID / BUNDLE_OBJECT_HASH`). Bundled objects are hashed, never parsed as policy or executed. The spec and
    87	    vectors objects are assembled by the part format of section 15.8. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G13]
    88	  - **Catalog entry** (one, for V1): the frozen object hashes; exactly one `alg` id (`OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256`
    89	    under the fallback, or the registered pair id under the hybrid); `alg_prohibited` = `[]`; `binding_forms` =
    90	    `["STMT_DIRECT"]`; D, δ, ε, k; DNSSEC algorithms {8, 13} and DS digest types {2, 4}. A well-formed `common.alg`
    91	    other than the catalog id, including the branch not taken, gives `UNVERIFIABLE / ALG_UNKNOWN`. The catalog is
    92	    independent of the bundle and of trust-configuration updates, and later verifiers apply it unchanged to V1
    93	    bundles (A9.4, A9.7 row 29). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G12]
    94	  - **Baseline.** The governing baseline is the frozen spec object hash in the catalog. A9 incorporates ENCODING-V1 at
    95	    its signing commit; a frozen edited ENCODING-V1 replaces it only with authorized change accounting.
    96	    [OWNER 2026-10-14, G37]
    97	- **Encoding:** `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md` at the signing commit, including D-1 to D-17. If the hybrid signer
    98	  branch is taken, the signing-commit baseline plus the dated branch-registration supplement governs. [A9:143-144;
    99	  A9:321-326]
   100	- **Mode:** strict only. One layer. No wrappers, no renewal, no TLR, no waiver policy. `VALID_DEGRADED` is never
   101	  returned. [A9:155; DD:67]
   102	- **Claim and sub-claims:** C1 to C7 as in A9:123-140. This document does not restate them.
   103	- **Authority:** DNSSEC for D plus the git key assertion. Both are required (n = 2). [A9:147; DD:65]
   104	- **Issuance:** an operated API (API Gateway, Lambda, KMS). A receipt ships only when complete. [A9:158-159]
   105	- **Parameters:** δ = 72 h, ε = 24 h, k = 6, N = 3, S = 24 h. The author's signature on A9 ratifies these five.
   106	  [A9:217-219] The verifier owns δ, ε and k; a receipt cannot choose them. [SPEC R-5.9:1219; SPEC R-3.46:698-700]
   107	  N and S govern the issuer only. δ, ε and k are frozen catalog constants, not trust-configuration data.
   108	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G12]
   109	- **Branch recorded:** hybrid or fallback signer branch. `OPEN (other):` not yet taken. The hybrid spike has a
   110	  21 Oct deadline; the owner records the branch, dated, in ENC §5.2 and in this document before the freeze.
   111	  [A9:298-326] Fallback: both slots OpenPGP P-256. Hybrid: slot `kms` ML-DSA-65, slot `gpg` OpenPGP P-256. (Still open, section 14.2 item 4.)
