   656	## 8. Signers and keys
   657	
   658	- Fallback: both slots OpenPGP P-256 (rule O), KMS-backed for kms, and slot-2 custody per A9.6 for gpg. The dated pre-freeze custody record identifies the selected implementation. [A9:338-340; A9.6 slot-2 custody, A9:341-360; ENC §5.2:438-444; `docs/reviews/a9-custody/` finding 3]
   659	- Hybrid, only if the spike passes by 21 Oct: `kms` is ML-DSA-65 (rule R), `gpg` is P-256 (rule O). One pair
   660	  algorithm id names both. [A9:298-302; ENC §5.2:441]
   661	- Key fingerprints: `spki-sha256:` for `kms`, `gpg-sha256:` for `gpg`. No SHA-1 for key binding. [ENC §3.3:285-301]
   662	- The two keys are separate technical failure domains under one controller. V1 claims no separation of control and no
   663	  independent fates. [A9:136; A9:368-372]
   664	- Each slot's signature is exactly one detached signature in the serialization its rule pins. [ENC §5.2:429-436]
   665	- **Transported keys.** `keys.gpg` is the bare v4 public-key packet body, exactly the `gpg-sha256` preimage (no
   666	  `0x99` prefix, packet header, user IDs, subkeys or armour). gpg must parse as the specified v4 P-256 public-key
   667	  body. kms must parse as P-256 DER SPKI under the fallback, or as the exact ML-DSA-65 SPKI specified by the dated
   668	  branch supplement under the hybrid. The rule is selected by the installed governing spec and slot, never by key
   669	  bytes alone. Otherwise `INVALID / KEY_FORMAT`; a key not hashing to its slot fingerprint is `INVALID /
   670	  KEY_MISMATCH`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G21]
   671	- **Rule-O signature policy** (attestation, possession and git signatures; OWNER CHOICE, supported-path limit)
   672	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G11]:
   673	  - ENC §5.2's grammar holds.
   674	  - Hashed area: exactly one signature-creation-time subpacket (type 2) with exactly four data octets, critical or
   675	    not, never compared with anything; no signature-expiration subpacket (type 3), critical or not; issuer key ID
   676	    (16) and issuer fingerprint (33) accepted critical or not and never read (no SHA-1 key binding, D-6); any other
   677	    type ignored if not critical and a failure if critical.
   678	  - Unhashed area: ignored entirely, critical bits included (ENC §3.5: the unhashed area carries no meaning).
   679	  - ECDSA per FIPS 186-5 with r, s ∈ [1, n−1]; low-s not required.
   680	  - Policy failure: `INVALID / SIG_POLICY`. Failed verification: `SIG_INVALID`, or `POSSESSION_INVALID` for the
   681	    manifest possession signatures. Possession proofs use the same per-slot rule over `F_manifest` (rule R for kms
   682	    under the hybrid). No revocation or current-time checks.
   683	  - *Dated correction 2026-10-14:* the resolutions draft's "no subpacket in either area has the critical bit set" is
   684	    withdrawn. RFC 9580 rejects only unknown critical subpackets and recommends a critical creation time; the blanket
   685	    ban rejected conforming signatures.
   686	- **Subpacket lengths.** RFC 9580 §5.2.3.7: first octet < 192, one octet; 192–254, two octets
   687	  `((o1−192)<<8)+o2+192` (192–16319); 255, four octets. The length counts the type octet and is ≥ 1. V1 accepts the
   688	  shortest form only (a V1 rule, not an RFC ban); a longer form is `SIG_FORMAT`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G28]
   689	- Revocation is not evaluated. Loss or theft handling is operations. [A9:248-252; RB §1]
