   725	## 10. Number rule
   726	
   727	Accept a number exactly when RFC 8785's canonical serialization preserves its value. Reject otherwise. The three
   728	conditions (not negative zero, finite after round-half-even, exact decimal value of `ES(d)` equals the literal) and
   729	the accepted and rejected examples are in ENC §1.2. [A9:438-443; ENC §1.2:118-148; ENC D-1:752-755] Proof:
   730	`formal/p8/PROOF.md` Lemma 3. Vectors: `formal/p8/vectors/`.
   731	
   732	This replaces the literal "exactly representable as an IEEE 754 double" rule for this profile only. [A9:405-406;
   733	A9:440-443] The stale "needs an author sentence" remarks in ENC (ENC:147-148, D-1) and PROOF §6 are superseded by
   734	A9.8. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G38; the ENC and PROOF wording edits are pending]
   735	
   736	**`ES` recipe.** `ES(d)` is ECMA-262 Number::toString of a pinned edition (edition, section and digest in the
   737	dependency manifest). If d is +0 or −0: `"0"`. If d < 0: `"-"` ‖ ES(−d). Otherwise let n, k, s be integers with
   738	k ≥ 1, 10^(k−1) ≤ s < 10^k, s × 10^(n−k) = d as a double, and k as small as possible; if several s qualify, choose
   739	the one for which s × 10^(n−k) is closest in value to d, and if two are equally close, the even one. Then: if
   740	k ≤ n ≤ 21, the k digits followed by n−k zeros; if 0 < n ≤ 21, the first n digits, `.`, the remaining k−n digits;
   741	if −6 < n ≤ 0, `0.`, −n zeros, the digits; otherwise the first digit, then `.` and the remaining digits if k > 1,
   742	then `e`, `+` or `-`, and abs(n−1) in decimal. Any formatter must reproduce N-01…N-22 and C-N01…C-N22; Python's
   743	`repr` is not ES. Unicode tables must be 16.0.0, identified by the UCD file digests in the dependency manifest; a
   744	runtime may use bundled pinned tables, and one whose tables do not match refuses to run (no verdict).
   745	[OWNER 2026-10-14, G29]
   746	
   747	**Field grammars.** `utc` years run 0001–9999 (proleptic Gregorian, seconds 00–59). LDH labels match
   748	`[a-z0-9-]{1,63}` with no leading or trailing hyphen; all-numeric labels, the top label included, are allowed; at
   749	least two labels; at most 241 bytes. This is what both P8 codecs already do. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G18; the ENC §3.2
   750	wording edit is pending]
