   900	### 15.2 OTS proofs and the txid [OWNER 2026-10-14, G20]
   901	
   902	OWNER CHOICE (supported-path limit). python-opentimestamps 0.4.5 is the reference reader, not normative.
   903	- **Header.** Magic `00 4f70656e54696d657374616d7073 0000 50726f6f66 00 bf89e2e884e89294`, varuint major version 1,
   904	  file-hash op `08` (SHA-256 only), the 32-byte digest, one Timestamp, end of input.
   905	- **Timestamp.** `Timestamp := (ff Item)* Item`; `Item := 00 Attestation | Op Timestamp`.
   906	- **Ops.** `08` (sha256), `f0 varbytes` (append), `f1 varbytes` (prepend). Arguments 1–4096 bytes; every message and
   907	  result at most 4096 bytes.
   908	- **Attestations.** `tag(8) varbytes(payload)`, payload at most 8192 bytes. Bitcoin `0588960d73d71901`: payload is
   909	  exactly one varuint height. Pending `83dfe30d2ef90c8e`: payload varbytes(URI ≤ 1000), URI ignored.
   910	- **Varuint.** LEB128, shortest form only, value ≤ 2^32 − 1. (python-opentimestamps 0.4.5 accepts redundant groups;
   911	  V1 does not.)
   912	- **Bounds.** Depth ≤ 256; ≤ 65536 ops and ≤ 4096 attestations per proof; proof ≤ 2^20 bytes. Duplicate identical
   913	  branches are permitted and have no effect.
   914	- **Rejections.** Any other op or tag, or any grammar or bound violation: `INVALID / OTS_FORMAT`. File digest must be
   915	  SHA256(`A_sig`) for the receipt (`RECEIPT_ANCHOR_MISMATCH`), SHA256 of the ENC §6 envelope for the snapshot
   916	  (`SNAPSHOT_STAMP_MISMATCH`), SHA256 of `<40-hex commit id>\n` for git (`GIT_STAMP_MISMATCH`).
   917	- **Merkle link.** A Bitcoin attestation's message is 32 bytes and equals bytes 36–68 of the bundled header at that
   918	  height.
   919	- **txid (supported-proof subset).** On the path to the **selected** attestation, let the first two consecutive
   920	  sha256 ops have input P, and let m be the message immediately before the maximal run of append/prepend ops that
   921	  precedes them. Required: (1) P parses exactly, consuming every byte, as a non-witness Bitcoin transaction —
   922	  version (4), compact-size input count ≥ 1, inputs (32 + 4 + compact-size script length + script + 4), compact-size
   923	  output count ≥ 1, outputs (8 + compact-size length + script), locktime (4); no SegWit marker; compact sizes
   924	  shortest form; (2) m is 32 bytes and some output script is exactly `6a 20 ‖ m`; (3) `hex(reverse(SHA256d(P)))`
   925	  equals `receipt_anchor.txid`. Otherwise `INVALID / ANCHOR_TXID_MISMATCH`. Any one path to the selected height may
   926	  satisfy this. (All 344 Bitcoin paths in the repository's 127 proofs have this shape, RES G20.)
   927	
   928	### 15.3 DNSSEC snapshot body [OWNER 2026-10-14, G19, G24, G30]
   929	
   930	A concatenation of RRs, each in RFC 1035 §3.2.1 wire format, uncompressed, in RFC 4034 §6.2 canonical form (owner
   931	name and every domain-name field inside RDATA, including the RRSIG signer name, lowercase and uncompressed).
   932	1. **Groups, in order:** the root DNSKEY group; then for each zone z below the root down to the TXT's signer zone, a
   933	   DS group at z and a DNSKEY group at z; last the TXT group at `_tessera-v1.<D>`. A group is a maximal run of RRs
   934	   with the same owner, CLASS IN, and TYPE t (the RRset) or TYPE RRSIG with Type Covered t (its witnesses). The RRset
   935	   comes first, in RFC 4034 §6.3 canonical RDATA order without duplicates, then zero or more RRSIGs in (key tag,
   936	   inception, expiration, signature bytes) order. Each z is a proper descendant of the previous zone. Signer names:
   937	   the parent for DS, z for DNSKEY, the root for the root group, the last z for TXT.
   938	2. **Fields.** CLASS IN. TTL equal within an RRset and otherwise uninterpreted; validation uses the RRSIG's Original
   939	   TTL.
   940	3. **Framing versus completeness.** A truncated RR encoding, forbidden RR type, duplicate RR, inconsistent
   941	   owner/type within a group, or misordered supplied group is `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`. A syntactically complete
   942	   sequence lacking a required RRset or its witness RRSIG is `UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING` (root:
   943	   `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`). Missing groups alone are not order violations. Forbidden: any type other than DNSKEY, DS,
   944	   TXT and RRSIG, and any RR at a name outside the chain; CNAME and DNAME are not followed. An empty body is
   945	   `LENGTH_CAP`.
   946	4. **Wildcards:** `INVALID / DNS_WILDCARD` (section 6.1).
   947	5. **Envelope:** ENC §6, `header ‖ u32 len ‖ body`, 1 ≤ len ≤ 2^24.
   948	
   949	### 15.4 Git evidence [OWNER 2026-10-14, G25]
   950	
   951	OWNER CHOICE (supported-path limit) plus SHA-1DC (BROADEN).
   952	- **Commit body** (without `commit <len>\0`): `tree <40 lhex>LF`, `(parent <40 lhex>LF)*`, `author <bytes>LF`,
   953	  `committer <bytes>LF`, exactly one `gpgsig <line>LF` with `( <line>LF)*` continuations, `LF`, message. Repeated
   954	  `parent` headers with distinct ids are allowed (merges); a repeated identical id, any other header (`encoding`,
   955	  `mergetag`, `gpgsig-sha256`, unknown), or a second `tree`, `author`, `committer` or `gpgsig` gives
   956	  `INVALID / GIT_COMMIT_FORMAT`. Author and committer are not interpreted. The signed payload is the commit without
   957	  the `gpgsig` line and its continuations (gitformat-signature(5)).
   958	- **Signature value** (continuations joined by LF, one leading space stripped from each): `-----BEGIN PGP
   959	  SIGNATURE-----` LF, one empty line, one or more base64 lines of 1–76 RFC 4648 characters (`=` padding only at the
   960	  end of the last), an optional CRC line `=` plus 4 base64 characters, `-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----`, no trailing LF.
   961	  No armor headers, no other blank lines, no whitespace inside lines. A present CRC-24 must match. Dearmored bytes
   962	  satisfy rule O's grammar and policy (section 8) with type 0x00. Otherwise `INVALID / GIT_SIG_FORMAT`.
   963	- **Trees.** Entries `mode SP name NUL id20`; modes {40000, 100644, 100755, 120000, 160000} without leading zero;
   964	  names nonempty, no `/` or NUL, not `.` or `..`; strictly sorted in git order (trees compare as `name/`), no
   965	  duplicates, body consumed exactly. Otherwise `INVALID / GIT_TREE_FORMAT`.
   966	- **Path.** Root entry `tessera-v1` (40000), then `key-assertion` (100644), the blob; `git.trees` is exactly
   967	  [root, sub]. Otherwise `INVALID / GIT_PATH`.
   968	- **Ids.** SHA-1 of `"<type> <len>\0" ‖ body` with collision detection (SHA-1DC); a detection is
   969	  `INVALID / GIT_SHA1_COLLISION`.
   970	- **Repository key.** v4 ECDSA P-256 public-key body, rule O (signer outcomes in section 6.3).
   971	- **Not checked:** that the commit introduced the blob.
