  1010	### 15.7 Total check order for the reported reason [OWNER 2026-10-14, G31, G26]
  1011	
  1012	Within a stage, subchecks in the order listed; per-slot checks in manifest slot order; per-member and per-candidate
  1013	checks in canonical (JCS key, then array index) order; per-height checks ascending.
  1014	1. Dispatch D1–D4.
  1015	2. Container: canonical JCS; absent members (first absent path); `git.object_format`; schema of present members
  1016	   (first offending path).
  1017	3. `a_sig` codec (ENC order).
  1018	4. Manifest codec; `manifest_sha256`.
  1019	5. Keys, per slot: `KEY_FORMAT`, `KEY_MISMATCH`.
  1020	6. Receipt consistency (ENC §5.3).
  1021	7. `ALG_UNKNOWN`.
  1022	8. `ISSUER_NOT_PINNED`; `SPEC_ID`; `SPEC_UNKNOWN`; `SPEC_OBJECT_MISMATCH`; binding forms (first offending element).
  1023	9. Signatures, per slot: `SIG_FORMAT`, `SIG_POLICY`, `SIG_INVALID`; then possession per slot.
  1024	10. Header pool, ascending height: `HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`, `HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`, `HEADER_CHAIN_BROKEN`.
  1025	11. Receipt OTS: `OTS_FORMAT`; `RECEIPT_ANCHOR_MISMATCH`; `OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH`; `HEADERS_MISSING` /
  1026	    `ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY`; `ANCHOR_TXID_MISMATCH`.
  1027	12. Conjuncts c1, c2, c3.
  1028	13. Snapshot: envelope and `LENGTH_CAP`; body (`SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`, `DNS_WILDCARD`); OTS (as 11, with
  1029	    `SNAPSHOT_STAMP_MISMATCH`, `SNAPSHOT_NOT_ANCHORED`); DNSSEC, root group, then each zone top-down, then TXT
  1030	    (section 5 and 6.1 outcomes, `DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING`); TXT record (ENC §7 order); `SNAPSHOT_TIME`.
  1031	14. Git: `GIT_COMMIT_FORMAT`; `GIT_SIG_FORMAT`; `GIT_TREE_FORMAT`; `GIT_SHA1_COLLISION`; `GIT_PATH`; OTS (as 11,
  1032	    with `GIT_STAMP_MISMATCH`, `GIT_NOT_ANCHORED`); `GIT_SIGNER_NOT_CONFIGURED` / `GIT_SIGNER_OUTSIDE_INTERVAL`;
  1033	    `GIT_NOT_PRECOMMITTED`.
  1034	15. `DNS_KEY_MISMATCH`, `CHANNEL_VALUE_MISMATCH`.
  1035	16. `ISSUANCE_WINDOW`.
  1036	17. `BUNDLE_OBJECT_HASH`.
  1037	
  1038	### 15.8 Spec and vectors object assembly [OWNER 2026-10-14, G13]
  1039	
  1040	Each object is one or more parts. A part is the ASCII line `tessera-v1-part <path> <length>` LF, then exactly
  1041	`<length>` bytes (decimal, no leading zeros), then LF. `<path>` is repository-relative UTF-8 without spaces. Parts are
  1042	in bytewise-sorted path order; file bytes verbatim as committed. The spec object holds the frozen
  1043	`docs/V1-PROFILE.md` and `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md` (plus the branch-registration supplement under the hybrid). The
  1044	vectors object holds every file under `formal/p8/vectors/` and the non-P8 conformance vectors (RES §L). The vectors
  1045	may embed the spec hash; the spec never embeds the vectors' hash.
