   246	The registered rejections "length-prefix mismatch" and "trailing bytes" are therefore one condition, reported by
   247	its direction. Once the length is the only payload boundary, a short length and a trailing byte are the same
   248	event.
   249	
   250	### 3.2 The attestation payload
   251	
   252	The payload is exactly this object. **No member may be missing or added** (`SCHEMA`). *Reason: a closed schema
   253	means no unsigned or unknown field can carry meaning, which is R-3.39.*
   254	
   255	```
   256	{"common":{
   257	   "alg":                 A,     ^[A-Z0-9][A-Z0-9-]{0,63}$          V1 issues "OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256"
   258	   "binding_forms":       [F…],  nonempty, strictly ascending, each ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,31}$
   259	   "content":             <any value in V>                          the requester's content
   260	   "declared_issue_time": "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ"                    a real UTC date and time, seconds 00–59
   261	   "issuer":              D,     lowercase LDH name, ≥ 2 labels, labels 1–63, total ≤ 241
   262	   "manifest_sha256":     hex64  hex(SHA256(manifest frame)), §4
   263	   "preamble_sha256":     hex64  hex(SHA256(purpose-preamble bytes))
   264	   "profile":             "tessera-v1-strict"                       exact
   265	   "spec":{"id": S,  ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._/-]{0,127}$                  V1: "tessera-v1-strict/verification-spec/1"
   266	           "sha256": hex64}      hex(SHA256(specification bytes))
   267	   "vectors_sha256":      hex64  hex(SHA256(conformance-vector bytes))
   268	 },
   269	 "signer":{"key_fp": FP}}        FP ∈ §3.3
   270	```
   271	
