   273	
   274	| Field | Reason, and the G-id it resolves |
   275	|---|---|
   276	| `alg`: any well-formed id, not only V1's | P8 accepts a well-formed unknown id, and stage (c) returns `UNVERIFIABLE`. The canary (R-3.53) needs this, and G-10b's failure mode is avoided. The id names the scheme: "a v4 OpenPGP binary-document signature whose document is the frame, ECDSA P-256, SHA-256" (G-57 kept). Its location inside the payload is A3 §A3.6.1's. G-11 is resolved for V1. |
