   750	## 9. Owner decisions taken here, for the author's record
   751	
   752	D-1 **Number rule: value-preserving (§1.2).** This changes A1 P8's item "numbers not exactly representable as
   753	IEEE 754 doubles" and prereg §4.3's "must be exactly representable". **It needs an A9 sentence.** Codex review 14
   754	asked for exactly that. The registered wording also fails to compose with RFC 8785 (§1.2). The derivation's
   755	profile line, which says the rule is unchanged, must be revised to match.
   756	D-2 Unicode 16.0.0 is pinned. Unassigned code points are rejected, and text that is not NFC is rejected rather than
   757	normalized.
   758	D-3 Limits: a payload of at most 2^24 bytes; depth 64 for the payload and 62 for content.
   759	D-4 Widths: a u8 tag length, a u16 canonicalization version equal to 1, and a u32 length (G-01 changed from u64).
   760	D-5 One tag for both signers' frames (A5 §A5.4). Slots are told apart by the fingerprint and the manifest order,
   761	and no slot name is written.
   762	D-6 Fingerprint strings carry scheme prefixes: `spki-sha256` for kms and `gpg-sha256` for gpg.
   763	**Owner decision (2026-10-09): no SHA-1 in V1.** The gpg key is bound by SHA-256 over its OpenPGP v4 public-key
   764	packet body, not by the v4 SHA-1 fingerprint, and this applies to the frame, the manifest and the DNS record. The
   765	KMS key stays SHA-256 of its SPKI. Its OpenPGP creation time is unbound, and that is accepted because the
   766	verifier binds the SPKI for that slot (§3.3).
   767	D-7 `manifest_sha256` is computed over the manifest frame. Spec, vectors and preamble are bound by SHA-256 of their
   768	raw bytes.
   769	D-8 *(revised 2026-10-12, findings 4 and 10)* The anchor preimage `A_sig` holds each slot's full frame and its
   770	exact detached signature, in manifest slot order, with a count byte, under the new tag
   771	`tessera-v1/receipt-anchor-sig`. The 2026-10-09 frame-only layout and its tag are withdrawn, with no fallback
   772	(§5.1). The DNSSEC snapshot has its own tagged envelope.
   773	D-9 A closed schema. `declared_issue_time` has second precision with no leap second. D is at most 241 characters.
   774	`binding_forms` is a sorted array.
   775	D-10 OpenPGP signature type 0x00 only. Since 2026-10-12, the anchor codec enforces this (§5.2, rule O).
   776	D-11 The dispatch boundary in §8.
   777	D-12 The DNS record: one RR, one string, a fixed order, no spaces, and the owner name compared without regard to
   778	case. Since 2026-10-12 every field is mandatory, so every canonical value is 255 bytes.
   779	D-13 Reason codes, and the order in which they are reported (§1.4, §3.1, §5, §7). "Trailing bytes" and
   780	"length-prefix mismatch" are reported as `TRAILING` or `TRUNCATED`, and this now includes a signature's own
   781	extent against its slot length. New in 2026-10-12:
   782	- `SIG_EMPTY`, `SIG_PACKET` and `SIG_FORMAT` (§5.2);
   783	- `LENGTH_CAP` for a signature above its cap;
   784	- the verification-stage codes of §5.3;
   785	- `DNS_WINDOW` (§7) and the C4 code `ISSUANCE_WINDOW` (§7.1);
   786	- `DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH` (§7; Amendment 9 disposition, 2026-10-12).
   787	
   788	D-14 *(2026-10-12)* Signature-slot rules are chosen by `(common.alg, slot)`. Rule O is one legacy-header binary v4
   789	packet of at most 1024 bytes. Rule R is raw FIPS 204/205 bytes of the exact parameter-set length. An unregistered
   790	id gets opaque bytes, 1 to 65536 of them.
   791	D-15 *(2026-10-12, finding 6)* The issue order is: frames, sign, verify, freeze the signature bytes, then stamp
   792	`A_sig` (§5.4).
   793	D-16 *(2026-10-12, finding 9)* The git channel's OTS stamp targets the signed commit's object id, never a tree, a
   794	blob or an unsigned commit (§7.2).
   795	D-17 *(2026-10-12, follow-up owner decision)* The issuance window lives in the key-publication record, in both
   796	channels. A receipt is `INVALID / ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless not-before ≤ declared time and T ≤ not-after. T is the
   797	registered header-time-derived T, with no margin. Key-format expiries are not relied on (§7.1). *Revised
   798	2026-10-12 (Amendment 9 disposition):* both bounds are mandatory and the window is at most 90 days
   799	(`DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH`).
