   298	
   299	## B. The time cluster: G03–G07, with G23
   300	
   301	One rule serves all three proofs: the receipt, the snapshot and the git commit.
   302	
   303	**Qualifying attestation.** A Bitcoin attestation at height h *qualifies* if and only if all of the following hold:
   304	- (a) the bundled header at h exists and its merkle root equals the attestation message;
   305	- (b) headers h, h+1, …, h+5 are all bundled (k = 6, `DepthK = 5`);
   306	- (c) each of those headers satisfies `hex(reverse(SHA256d(header))) = pin[height]`;
   307	- (d) for i = h+1…h+5, `header_i.prev = SHA256d(header_{i−1})`.
   308	
   309	**Selection rule (F02 text).** "Attestation selection is existential over qualifying branches. A syntactically valid
   310	Bitcoin attestation without a complete h..h+5 segment is nonqualifying, not a required failed check. It supplies no
   311	time or trust fact. All supplied headers, including unused ones, are independently checked against pins. For each
   312	adjacent supplied pair at consecutive heights, the prev-hash link must match. Missing heights are not a broken-link
   313	failure. The selected anchor, rather than every unverified attestation, is the referent of 'anchors beyond the newest
   314	pin.'" A9 C6 now registers this reading (OWNER DECISION 2026-10-14, F02).
   315	
   316	**Header-pool checks** (shared pool, every supplied header, used or not):
   317	- **G23.** A supplied header at a pinned height with a different hash: `INVALID / HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`.
   318	- **A9 rule.** A supplied header at a height with **no** pin: `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`.
   319	- **Linkage.** For each pair of supplied headers at consecutive heights, a prev-hash mismatch gives
   320	  `INVALID / HEADER_CHAIN_BROKEN`. A missing intermediate height is not a broken link.
   321	- **Asymmetry, stated.** At an unselected height q, a present, correct, pinned inclusion header with missing
   322	  successors is ignored (the branch is nonqualifying). A present **unpinned** header at q blocks the whole bundle
   323	  (`UNVERIFIABLE`) by the pin rule above.
   324	
   325	**Proof-level outcomes**, evaluated over every Bitcoin attestation in the proof:
   326	- **Contradiction gives INVALID.** A supplied header at h that is pinned and whose merkle root ≠ the attestation
   327	  message gives `INVALID / OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH`.
   328	- **No qualifying attestation.** If any Bitcoin attestation is present, `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_MISSING`. If the
   329	  proof has only pending attestations, `UNVERIFIABLE / ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY`. The snapshot uses its own code,
   330	  `SNAPSHOT_NOT_ANCHORED`, and git uses `GIT_NOT_ANCHORED`.

